# This site (started from Eleventy Excellent, restyled by Tabula Rasa)

- Read **`docs/eleventy-excellent-reference.md`** for the layouts, the CSS files, config layout, `{% svg %}`, and images.
- **Layouts:** the `base`, `page`, and `post` aliases point at `src/_layouts/rasa.njk`, `rasa-page.njk`, and `rasa-post.njk`. Header, footer, home stream, and cards live in `src/_includes/rasa/`.
- **CSS:** plain CSS in `src/assets/css/rasa/`, built with postcss-import and cssnano only. Include it with `{% css "rasa" %}{% include "css/rasa-<file>.css" %}{% endcss %}`; the layout inlines the bucket. No Tailwind, no utility classes, no CUBE layers, no token JSON.
- **Colours:** use the six custom properties in `site.css` (`--bg`, `--text`, `--muted`, `--rule`, `--accent`, `--card`), which flip for dark mode. Headings `--font-hand` (Caveat), body `--font-body` (`system-ui`), code `--font-code`.
- Netlify caches `/assets/*` for a month, so new CSS goes in the inline bucket or gets a new filename.
- Older plans in `docs/` name `src/assets/css/local/` and `global/`. Those are gone; follow this repo's `src/pages/`, `src/posts/`, and `eleventy.config.js`.
